Package: eco
Type: Package
Title: Access Ecological Detection Data from the eco Warehouse
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
  person("Ben", "Domingue", email = "ben.domingue@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
  )
Description: Find, download and reshape tables from eco, an IRW-style warehouse
    of ecological detection data (occupancy, repeated counts, capture histories,
    community surveys) in one long format with columns unit, taxon and y. Tables
    are read from the public Redivis dataset 'datapages.eco' over its anonymous
    CSV endpoint, so no account or token is needed. Converters turn a long table
    into the site-by-occasion arrays, 'unmarked' frames and capture-history
    strings the ecological model packages expect, and back.
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports:
    data.table,
    jsonlite,
    methods,
    tools,
    utils
Suggests:
    arrow,
    curl,
    knitr,
    redivis,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0),
    unmarked
